      "review_summary": "The PR centralizes repair-worker timeout budgeting, raises the worker, execute-step, and job defaults to 30/70/75 minutes, reserves capacity for later workers, and adds focused workflow and budget tests.\n\nReproducibility: yes. On this exact head, set `CLAWSWEEPER_FIX_STEP_TIMEOUT_MS` above 4,200,000 milliseconds; the helper accepts values through 7,200,000 milliseconds even though the enclosing workflow step ends after 70 minutes, directly reproducing the reported deadline mismatch from source.",
      "review_followup": "- [P2] The autofix-opted PR has one narrow mechanical blocker that an automated worker can repair by aligning accepted timeout bounds with the fixed workflow deadlines and extending focused boundary coverage.",
